  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 238633,
  "published": "2026-08-02T13:17:33.97Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.0.0-alpha.13: the fourth caller-settable trust assertion leaves the bindable registration DTO, plus three permission-matrix correctness fixes -- read UPGRADE.md 26 before upgrading. SOURCE-BREAKING: MyIdentityRegisterDTO.TenantId no longer exists, so code that sets or nulls it will not compile; the tenant now travels as an int? tenantId argument on the server-side RegisterAsync overload, which grew from 5 to 6 parameters (int? tenantId before CancellationToken) and validates that the tenant exists and is active before creating anything. Delete any hand-written sanitisation such as registerDto.TenantId = null: a public self-registration endpoint can no longer name a tenant at all. This is also BINARY-BREAKING for the 5-argument overload, and an implementer of IMyIdentityAuthenticationService or a subclass overriding that overload must add the parameter. Behaviour changes: AssignToTenantAsync refuses a deactivated destination tenant with the new MyIdentityErrorCodes.TenantInactive instead of silently stranding the user; SaveRolePermissionsAsync rejects a request naming one catalog module under two spellings with the new MyIdentityErrorCodes.AmbiguousModuleCode instead of leaking a raw DbUpdateException, and now resolves and validates every module BEFORE invoking OnBeforePermissionsRemovedAsync, so an unknown module code or an unsupported flag throws without the hook running. Fixed: the removal diff passed to OnBeforePermissionsRemovedAsync is now computed store-side, so the database collation -- not C# ordinal equality -- decides which rows the request keeps; persisted MyIdentityRolePermission.ModuleCode is now the catalog's canonical spelling rather than the caller's. Added: MyIdentityMessageDescriber.CannotAssignToInactiveTenant(), CannotCreateUserInInactiveTenant() and AmbiguousModuleCodeInRequest(). API may still change before stable.",
